<http://data.silknow.org/object/be828cea-7d08-3769-bbf1-d4f41053235d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Wallet or stocking purses were very popular up to the 1860s, and they survive in great numbers, although examples of frame-knitted (machine) purses are rare.  Many stocking purses were netted in silk and had steel beads, spangles and paillettes with steel, gilt, silver or gold sliders and tassels; their decoration varied from the minimal to highly patterned.  Often they were inscribed and dated, many, like this one, were made as gifts for gentlemen."@en , "Beaded stocking purse, crocheted in blue silk and steel beads, inscribed Samuel Stockford, with two cut steel rings, tassel and fringe"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/751abbe7-6871-3364-9bc4-f3c880493b93> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/7d86a400-be0c-3502-96b0-76993b8035ad> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Wallet or stocking purses were very popular up to the 1860s, and they survive in great numbers, although examples of frame-knitted (machine) purses are rare.  Many stocking purses were netted in silk and had steel beads, spangles and paillettes with steel, gilt, silver or gold sliders and tassels; their decoration varied from the minimal to highly patterned.  Often they were inscribed and dated, many, like this one, were made as gifts for gentlemen."@en , "Beaded stocking purse, crocheted in blue silk and steel beads, inscribed Samuel Stockford, with two cut steel rings, tassel and fringe"@en ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.1194-1913" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O75498> .

